==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tʌb/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌb|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[flat]]-[[bottomed]] [[vessel]], of width similar to or greater than its height, used for [[storing]] or [[packing]] things, or for [[washing]] things in.
#: ''He bought a '''tub''' of lard to roast the potatoes in.''
# The [[content]]s or [[capacity]] of such a vessel.
#: ''He added a '''tub''' of margarine to the stew.''
# A [[bathtub]].
# {{context|nautical|informal|lang=en}} A [[slow]]-[[moving]] [[craft]].
# {{context|humorous|or|derogatory|lang=en}} Any structure shaped like a tub, such as a certain old form of [[pulpit]], a short broad [[boat]], etc.
#* South
#*: All being took up and busied, some in pulpits and some in '''tubs''', in the grand work of preaching and holding forth.
# A small [[cask]].
#: ''a '''tub''' of gin''
# {{context|mining|lang=en}} A box or bucket in which [[coal]] or [[ore]] is sent up a [[shaft]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[sweat]]ing in a tub; a [[tub fast]].
#: {{rfquotek|Shakespeare}}
# {{cx|slang|lang=en}} A corpulent or obese person.
#: '''Lars''': You ready to help take down Gizmo?<br/>'''Vault Dweller''': You bet. Let's nail that '''tub'''. [http://fallout.wikia.com/wiki/LARS.MSG]

